## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests CDS governance, real-world guardrails, and Azure AI integration.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant prompts
- PII redaction and safety checks
- Governance metadata and provenance
- Audit logging to Data Lake
- Fallback policies and test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// example wrapper pseudocode for gating
async function respond(input, tenantId){
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const ctx = await fetchContext(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(ctx, redacted);
  const risk = await safetyCheck(prompt);
  if(!risk.ok) return fallbackResponse(ctx);
  const res = await openaiChat(prompt);
  const final = attachGovernance(res, tenantId, ctx.modelVer);
  await log(final);
  return final;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the end-to-end logging and searchability of prompts? 
- How would you handle model version rollouts with zero-downtime for tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests knowledge of Azure OpenAI integration, policy-based gating, and tenant isolation in a practical chat app.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-policy retrieval from Azure Key Vault
- Input screening with Azure Text Analytics
- Policy gating before Azure OpenAI calls
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and KB in Blob
- Per-tenant auditing to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
async function handle(input, tenantId){
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId)
  if(!passesPolicy(input, policy)) return cannedReply(policy)
  const grounded = groundKB(input)
  return await openAiQuery(grounded)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test different policy rules per tenant?
- How would you handle policy updates without redeploying services?"

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design secure, scalable, multi-tenant AI-assisted incident triage on Azure with data governance.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Multi-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- PII redaction and compliance
- Canary deployment and rollback
- Audit logs and data lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch of flow stages
async function handleEvent(e) {
  const norm = normalize(e);
  const doc = await kbQuery(norm, tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(doc, norm);
  const resp = await openai.infer(prompt);
  const safe = redact(resp);
  await logAudit({tenantId, event: e, resp: safe});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the sandboxing to prevent prompt injection in a CI/CD pipeline?
- Which metrics and SLAs would you monitor to ensure per-tenant quota enforcement doesn't throttle critical alerts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect a multi-tenant Azure OpenAI flow integrated with DevOps, covering data lineage, security, and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI + API Management
- Cognitive Search KB in Blob
- Per-tenant RBAC (Azure AD)
- PII redaction (Text Analytics)
- Data Lake logging
- Canary deployments and end-to-end latency goals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestration snippet showing tenant context, diff->prompt, and moderation
async function reviewPR(prDiff, tenantId){
  const kb = await loadKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(prDiff, kb, tenantId);
  const review = await openAiReview(prompt);
  if(hasPIIRisk(review)){ redact(review); }
  await storeLogs(tenantId, {prDiff, review});
  return review.comments;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and monitor prompt drift across tenants without leaking data?
- What latency and cost controls would you put in place for high-velocity repos?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a scalable, compliant incident-response assistant that isolates tenants, enforces cost controls, and integrates with Azure Monitor, Cognitive Search, RBAC, and auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant sandboxed OpenAI deployments behind API Management
- Event-driven ingestion from Azure Monitor
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- RBAC with Azure AD and Data Lake auditing
- Canary rollout and end-to-end tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing function outline
async function handleIncident(event) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(event);
  const doc = await kbSearch(tenant, event);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(doc, event);
  const redacted = redactPII(prompt);
  const res = await openaiQuery(tenant, redacted);
  await logAudit(tenant, event, res);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for latency under peak load?
- How would you ensure data residency per tenant across regions?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes architectural decisions for multi-tenant Azure AI deployments with strict data residency, governance, and explainability requirements. It tests ability to plan region-aware routing, tenant-scoped knowledge bases, identity boundaries, and end-to-end auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency and customer-managed keys (CMK) for storage
- Region-local Cognitive Search indexes per tenant
- Region-aware model routing for Azure OpenAI
- Per-tenant RBAC using Azure AD
- Explainability logging to Data Lake with traceability
- End-to-end testing including latency, privacy, and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo region routing for tenants
function getTenantRegion(tenantId) {
  const regionMap = {
    't1': 'eastus',
    't2': 'northeurope'
  };
  return regionMap[tenantId] || 'eastus';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate cross-region consistency and prove data residency?
- What failure modes require circuit breakers and fallback paths, and how would you implement them?

